   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening leadership</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pauline Suvi, who heads up the science department at Papua New Guinea&#x2019;s Sogeri National School of Excellence, completed a Queensland University of Technology (QUT) Graduate Certificate in Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics (STEM) Education in 2023 under the Australia Awards program. Since completing her course, Pauline has collaborated with QUT on its forthcoming publication on the importance of integrated STEM education in Papua New Guinea, co-authoring a chapter on increasing the participation of girls in STEM related subjects. In fact, Pauline is one of 18 high performing Papua New Guinean awardees whose best practice in the classroom will be showcased in the publication, demonstrating the positive impact of ongoing teacher professional training on local practices. The publication will be a valuable contribution to advancing the STEM agenda and collaborative teaching approaches in Papua New Guinea.</narrative>
    </description>
